# BACKGROUND PARTICLE EFFECT:```
What the interactive background is.
It is a canvas based particle system with a soft glow orb.
Particles float slowly.
Particles react to cursor movement.
Nearby particles connect with animated lines.
A large radial glow follows the cursor slightly.
Everything resizes automatically for screen size.

This effect has three layers.

Full screen canvas for particles.

Fixed glow orb for depth.

Website content above both layers.

Layer 1. Particle canvas.
You add a canvas element as the first element inside body.

canvas id particle-canvas

CSS rules.
• position fixed
• top 0 left 0
• width 100 percent
• height 100 percent
• pointer-events none
• low z-index

Why this matters.
Canvas stays behind content.
Mouse clicks pass through.
Animation never blocks UI.

Layer 2. Particle logic.
Particles are JavaScript objects.

Each particle stores.
• x and y position
• speed in x and y
• size
• opacity
• pulse value
• hue color

Animation loop.
• Clear canvas every frame.
• Update particle position.
• Apply slow floating movement.
• Add pulse using sine wave.
• Push particles away from cursor if close.
• Wrap particles when they leave screen.
• Draw particle glow using radial gradient.
• Draw particle core circle.

Cursor interaction.
Mouse position is tracked globally.
If cursor is within 150px of a particle.
Particle is gently pushed away.
This creates the responsive feel.

Particle connections.
Every frame checks distance between particles.
If distance is under 150px.
Draw a thin line between them.
Line opacity depends on distance.
Line color blends both particle colors.

Performance safety.
Particle count depends on screen size.
Large screens get more particles.
Small screens get fewer particles.

Layer 3. Glow orb.
This is a pure CSS element.

HTML structure.
div class glow-orb-wrapper
div class glow-orb

CSS behavior.
• Fixed at screen center.
• Large circular radial gradient.
• Very low opacity.
• Infinite pulse animation using scale and opacity.

Cursor effect.
JavaScript shifts the wrapper slightly.
Movement range is about 30px.
This creates parallax depth.

Why orb feels smooth.
It does not track cursor directly.
It moves slower and less distance.
Your eyes see depth, not jitter.

Reduced motion support.
System checks prefers-reduced-motion.
If enabled.
Canvas animation stops.
Canvas clears.
This avoids motion issues.

How to reuse this on another website.

Step 1. Copy required files.
• Copy the canvas element.
• Copy glow orb HTML.
• Copy particle JS section only.
• Copy canvas and glow CSS.

Step 2. Order matters.
Canvas must be before your content.
Glow orb must be after canvas.
Main content must have higher z-index.

Step 3. Minimal CSS setup.
Body must allow fixed elements.
Do not set overflow hidden unless needed.
Content container should use position relative and higher z-index.

Step 4. Customize safely.
To change density.
Adjust particleCount formula.

To change color.
Change particle hue values.
Change glow orb gradient colors.

To change interaction strength.
Adjust mouse distance threshold.
Adjust force multiplier.

To disable connections.
Remove drawConnections call.

Step 5. Mobile behavior.
This system already scales particles down.
Canvas auto resizes on window resize.
Touch devices still work without cursor force.

Common mistakes to avoid.
• Forgetting pointer-events none on canvas.
• Putting canvas inside a container instead of body.
• Using too many particles on large screens.
• Not handling prefers-reduced-motion.


